  "aboutVisibleRangeTitle": "About visible range",
  "aboutWallpaperTitle": "About grouped wallpaper",
  "aboutVisibleRangeWhat": "1. What the visible range is\n• It decides which photos and videos the gallery browsing shows. Files are not moved, copied or hidden elsewhere.\n• It applies to the collection, album list, tags, places, formats, search suggestions, counts and covers.\n• It does not change the grouped wallpaper. Wallpaper groups have their own ranges and their own browsing toggle.\n• The gallery has one visible range. Only wallpaper groups have several.",
  "aboutVisibleRangeParts": "2. The three parts\n• Base range (exclusive): the first item, Unrestricted, is fixed and cannot be deleted. The rest comes from the built-in presets or from ranges you save.\n• Additional restrictions (AND): narrow the base further. Built-in restrictions are listed here switched off.\n• Supplements (OR): add back what was filtered out. Built-in supplements are listed here switched off. Depending on the group order they are shown as supplements outside the base or inside the restrictions.\n• Group order: restrictions before supplements, or supplements before restrictions. Each visible range saves its own.\n• Every step shows its count. The current visible range at the bottom shows every active condition.\n• Switching the base keeps the restrictions and supplements.",
  "aboutVisibleRangeRestricted": "3. Unrestricted and restricted\n• Unrestricted: the base is Unrestricted and no additional restriction group exists. Supplements do not change this.\n• Restricted: the base is not Unrestricted, or at least one additional restriction group exists.\n• Example: Unrestricted base with only a supplement is still Unrestricted, because the result is still everything; a supplement only changes the final set.\n• The same rule labels the wallpaper page's Available wallpaper and Available wallpaper (browsing restricted).",
  "aboutVisibleRangeActivate": "4. Activating and editing\n• Long press a rule to start selecting. With one rule selected, More can move it to the base, restrictions or supplements, open the media set with it (replace or append), or rename it.\n• Multi-selection, including a single rule, can be deleted.\n• Activating only changes the media set's browsing filters. It does not bypass the visible range; an empty result is shown as empty.\n• Every activation records a session. When you save, you can write one session back: only the filters it added or removed are applied to its rule.\n• Any save (a range, a rule, a wallpaper group) clears every session, whether or not you wrote one back.",
  "aboutVisibleRangeLock": "5. Locking and permissions\n• The floating button locks or unlocks. A detailed lock sets permissions before locking.\n• The default is read-only with sharing allowed. Each visible range can set deleting, editing, vault, recycle bin and metadata permissions.\n• While locked the range cannot be switched or edited, and entries that would bypass the filter are filtered instead.\n• The lock is protection against casual peeking inside this app, not a security boundary. It does not encrypt or otherwise change your files. Clearing app data, using another app or root can still bypass it, but at least you will know it was not an accident.",
  "aboutVisibleRangeWallpaper": "6. Relation to wallpaper\n• Visible ranges and wallpaper groups are saved separately. With the wallpaper browsing effect on, browsing is the visible range AND the current wallpaper group, so both constrain it.\n• Wallpaper group 0 means no wallpaper group effect. Groups 1..n each have their own visible range.\n• Wallpaper only uses images; videos do not participate.\n• Available wallpaper and Available wallpaper (browsing restricted) describe whether gallery browsing is restricted, not whether the wallpaper itself is limited.",
  "aboutVisibleRangeDefaults": "7. Defaults and restoring\n• Built-in candidates cover all three sections: base candidates are presets, restriction and supplement candidates are rules listed switched off.\n• Re-add defaults restores the built-in presets and rules, deduping by id and by filter fingerprint.\n• You can customize every base, restriction and supplement: built-in base presets are read-only, while a built-in rule can be switched on, renamed or deleted like your own.",
  "aboutWallpaperWhat": "What this is\n• Grouped wallpaper is an Aves + Muzei live wallpaper.\n• It is equivalent to a Muzei wallpaper source: all images plus the current wallpaper group's visible range.\n• Videos do not participate. They are hidden like in Muzei and never shown as filter chips.",
  "aboutWallpaperMuzei": "Relation to Muzei\n• Both are live wallpapers built on the same technical base. They are independent, but only one can be active at a time.\n• Enabling grouped wallpaper replaces Muzei; enabling Muzei replaces grouped wallpaper.\n• This feature does not support a single wallpaper. For that, use the Muzei wallpaper settings.",
  "aboutWallpaperGroups": "Wallpaper groups\n• Group 0 = no wallpaper group effect. It never changes the current wallpaper and is not a single-image mode.\n• Groups 1..n each keep an independent visible range: base, restrictions, supplements and order.\n• The defaults are 1/2/3: 1 all, 2 the Pictures path, 3 the DCIM path. They are demonstrations and can be changed.\n• Switching to a group with no images does nothing.\n• The notification cycles only the enabled groups 1..m; the current group is the one the actual wallpaper uses.\n• Group 0 is fixed first and is never numbered or dragged. 1..m is the enabled section, m+1..n the disabled section; dragging works inside a section.\n• Deleting or disabling the current group falls back to 0 and leaves the wallpaper unchanged until another group is chosen.\n• Numbers are automatic and cannot be edited. The current group follows its content, and the notification updates with it.",
  "aboutWallpaperAvailability": "Available wallpaper / Available wallpaper (browsing restricted)\n• This describes whether gallery browsing is restricted, not the wallpaper.\n• Available wallpaper: the base is Unrestricted and there is no additional restriction group. Supplements do not affect this.\n• Available wallpaper (browsing restricted): the base is not Unrestricted, or at least one additional restriction group exists.\n• While the visible range is unlocked, the wallpaper page's More can temporarily remove or restore the restriction. It only affects browsing on the wallpaper page and is restored when you leave; the actual wallpaper is unaffected.\n• A locked visible range cannot be temporarily removed.",
  "aboutWallpaperSync": "Syncing and resetting\n• Edits on the wallpaper page are a draft. Syncing to wallpaper is what actually bakes it; reset returns to the actual wallpaper.\n• Activating a rule only changes the browsing filters and never bypasses the visible range.",
  "aboutVisibleRangeOrderNote": "Visible range notes come first on the visible range page; wallpaper notes come first on the wallpaper page. Both pages can read everything.",

